# --- Trees that must never enter the build context ---

# The Cloudflare tunnel token. Nothing in the image needs it (it is mounted
# into the cloudflared container as a Docker secret at runtime), and a build
# context copy lands in an intermediate layer.
secrets

# ETL output and source video: 800 MB and 13 GB respectively, neither of which
# `npm run build` reads. out/ reaches the container as a read-only mount, not a
# COPY. Leaving these in the context made every image build stream the whole
# lot to the daemon, and a single unreadable .MOV fail the build outright.
out
raw
models

# Python side: the ETL runs on the host, never in the web image.
.venv
.venv313
__pycache__

# Scratch trees left behind by an interrupted test run.
.test-tmp*
